id: pm-rust-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and full deep tiers
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required Rust platform checks and the release aggregate, split quick PR work from full deep gates, retain complete coverage thresholds, and certify routing and depth controls."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: ci,performance
created_at: "2026-11-16T05:26:56.154Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T05:42:59.281Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Preserve all required contexts and original checks; prove deterministic quick depth and bounded jobs; record measured CI and release claim.
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T05:26:58.811Z",codex-sol,"Initial audit: required contexts verified as Rust ubuntu-latest, Rust macos-latest, Rust windows-latest and Release gate aggregate; CodeQL is not required. No existing open CI v2 item found. Plan: quick deterministic corpora and property counts; parallel Linux release components with an always-running strict aggregate; full npm/Bun and OS gates in deep. Preserve release workflows and verifier scripts."
  "2026-11-16T05:35:40.449Z",codex-sol,"Baseline run 43729555388: Rust execution Linux 790s, macOS 863s, Windows 1364s; full aggregates Linux npm 1610s, Bun 2376s, macOS 2073s, Windows 3236s. Slow Linux targets: claim/release 180.71s, orientation 138.80s, pagination 108.38s, search/collections 83.77s. Implemented two disjoint platform target shards, fail-closed required aggregates, parallel Linux quick release components, unchanged full-scope 100% LLVM coverage, deterministic quick property prefixes and kind-preserving focused crash replays. Deep keeps complete original gates and unscaled latency budgets. Local setup is user-space and locked; cold WAN tool bootstrap and ptrace still need runner evidence."
  "2026-11-16T05:42:58.787Z",codex-sol,"Initial local validation passed: cargo check and clippy on all targets/features; fmt; typed harness typecheck/lint; two partition/identity fixtures; 12 documentation contracts; unchanged changelog; strict YAML with duplicate-key rejection; shell parsing. Strict health passes with a clean HOME and installed merge drivers: the inherited-home extension skew was local configuration, not a repository defect. Touched quick-depth Rust suites are still running; no full local suite or coverage claim. Publishing early for hosted validation."
